  "note": "Independent re-audit against RFC 9494 Section 4.2 and current gr.go/gr_state.go (post-18b491ae23). Section 4.2 requires retaining stale routes after session down and before re-establishment, bounded by Restart Time + Long-Lived Stale Time (including zero-GR immediate LLGR, omitted-GR deemed zero, and both-zero base BGP). onSessionDownPlan preserves identical first-DOWN retention and immediate-entry scheduling; in handleLLSTExpired, while the session is down (syncing==false, llstExpiredDuringSync empty), lastFamily expiry still deletes peer state and fires onLLGRFamilyExpired + onLLGRComplete. All 10 tagged units verified: real-RIB tests TestRFC9494ZeroRestartTimeRetainsThroughTheLLGRPeriod, TestRFC9494RestartTimeThenLongLivedStaleTime, TestRFC9494DelayedDownPreservesLLSTDeadlines, TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyRetainsRealRIB, TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyTimerSurvivesConventionalEntry, and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyReadvertisementDoesNotDelaySiblingExpiry verify GR level-1 -> LLGR level-2 + LLGR_STALE retention and 1ns virtual-clock boundaries on both JSON and structured paths; negatives TestOnTimerExpired_WithoutLLGR, TestRFC9494BothTimesZeroRetainsNothing, and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyWithoutLLSTIsRemoved verify deletion without LLGR or with zero/unexchanged LLST; TestLLSTTimerExpiry_LastFamily supplements state-manager coverage.",
